These findings are not architecture-specific: embedding co-adaptation may interact pathologically with value estimation in any imagination-based actor-critic that bootstraps within a learned model.

\paragraph{Practical implications.}
\label{sec:detector}
\looseness=-1 Three guidelines follow. (1)~Monitor NVE throughout training: a sustained rise above $2.0\times$ indicates CIVO onset (online detector: TPR~$5/5$, FPR~$2/9$; Algorithm~\ref{alg:civo_detector}, Appendix~\ref{sec:detector_appendix}). (2)~Use frozen-embedding runs as a diagnostic control: if frozen matches trained, the embedding fuels co-adaptation rather than temporal reasoning. (3)~Wide dual-critic (min $+$ capacity) is the only partial prevention (3/4); scaling this approach or decoupling the embedding from value prediction represent promising directions for future research.

